The inspector toggle is a toolbar item macOS 14 supplies for .toggleInspector. On macOS 11 the toolbar's delegate
makes it (the identifier is AppKitCompat's .compatToggleInspector): a button for toggleAppInspector, the View
menu's Show Inspector.

diff --git a/LightTouchMac/UI/MainWindowController+Toolbar.swift b/LightTouchMac/UI/MainWindowController+Toolbar.swift
index 88ecde05..7499d85d 100644
--- a/LightTouchMac/UI/MainWindowController+Toolbar.swift
+++ b/LightTouchMac/UI/MainWindowController+Toolbar.swift
@@ -126,6 +126,9 @@ extension MainWindowController {
             return item
         case .zoom:
             return makeZoomToolbarItem()
+        case .compatToggleInspector:
+            // Big Sur port: macOS 14 supplies this item itself; macOS 11 gets the View menu's toggle as a button.
+            return button(id, "Inspector", "sidebar.right", #selector(toggleAppInspector(_:)), "Show or Hide the Inspector")
         case .compatInspectorTrackingSeparator:
             // Must be supplied explicitly with the split view and the divider
             // it tracks. Listing the identifier alone got it silently dropped,
